   "text": {
    "L1": "Plants are grouped by their stems, not by height alone.",
    "L2": "A herb has a soft, green stem and is usually short.",
    "L3": "A shrub has hard, woody stems that branch near the ground.",
    "L4": "A tree has one thick, hard, woody trunk, with branches higher up.",
    "L5": "So a tall banana plant is still a herb because its stem is soft.",
    "L6": "A young mango sapling is still a tree because it grows into one woody trunk.",
    "L7": "The height clue can help, but the stem is the real test.",
    "L8": "Now classify plants by checking the stem and the branching pattern."
   },
